# Rank 1697 / CVE-2022-31099: rulex compiles its own regex language to
# regexes through a hand-written recursive-descent parser, and the descent
# had no depth budget. parse_modified calls parse_or, parse_or calls
# parse_sequence, parse_sequence calls parse_fixes, and parse_fixes
# re-enters parse_modified (lookaround and group arms) and itself (the
# `Token::Not` fix arm), so every nesting level of the input -- each `(((`,
# each `!!`, each lookaround -- costs another turn around a four-function
# call cycle on the native stack, and a short deeply-nested expression
# aborts the process with a stack overflow (denial of service through
# uncontrolled recursion, CWE-400/CWE-674). The fixing commit is 60aa2dc0 ("Add
# recursion limit") threads a `recursion: u16` through the parser Input:
# Rulex::parse passes 256, a local `recurse` wrapper around each
# re-entry point calls Input::recursion_start, which does
# `self.recursion.checked_sub(1).ok_or(RecursionLimit)`, and recursion_end
# restores the budget on the way out. Verified in both directions: the
# parent (330b353) carries the full unbounded cycle and no counter, and
# the fixed revision carries recursion_start/recursion_end plus the 256 at the entry
# (lib.rs:87, input.rs:40, parsers.rs:97/105/156/167/303). No pool
# correction.
#
# What fires today: nothing, on either revision. `scan --cache off` over
# the parent reports 43 findings (18 VYQL-MEM-005, 22 VYQL-MEM-006,
# 2 VYQL-PATH-001, 1 VYQL-CFG-014 -- deref/subscript heuristics in
# features.rs, range.rs, group.rs, token.rs) and the fixed tree reports 46
# of the same families, none in rulex-lib/src/parse/parsers.rs at either
# revision. `vyql match` on the vulnerable parsers.rs labels exactly five
# code.IndexAccessSink nodes, all inside parse_quoted_text (lines 586-623)
# -- nothing on any member of the recursive cycle.
#
# Why no binding can express the discriminating question, measured:
#
# (1) The cycle is mutual across four functions, so no single function
#     context contains it. The Rust frontend emits per-function
#     call:/call_path:/call_arg: tokens (rust.go rsStructuredContextTokens)
#     and no fact for a call-graph cycle; the one direct self-call
#     (parse_fixes -> parse_fixes at the `Token::Not` arm) is present at
#     BOTH revisions -- the fixed revision wraps it in recurse(parse_fixes) rather
#     than removing it -- so even a self-recursion label discriminates
#     nothing here.
# (2) A presence binding cannot ask "does this function call itself"
#     at all: predicate right sides must be string literals
#     (internal/bindings/compile_presence.go:236), so
#     node.context.name == node.context.call does not compile. This is
#     1320's C measurement, reconfirmed on the current engine for Rust.
# (3) The budget itself is delegated out of the file: the comparison
#     lives in Input::recursion_start in input.rs, the cap value (256) is
#     passed at Rulex::parse in lib.rs, and within parsers.rs the only
#     trace of the remediation is calls to the fixed revision's own new `recurse`
#     helper. A binding keyed on recurse/recursion_start fails the rename
#     test -- it is the fixing commit's vocabulary, not API vocabulary
#     (the generic shape, "budgeted by an argument passed at the entry",
#     is satisfied by spelling the wrapper anything at all). The
#     delegated-check invisibility is 1364's Rust family.
# (4) The nearest concepts are each library-bound with no Rust binding
#     and none expresses "recursive descent without a depth budget":
#     RecursiveCompressedPacketDecompression (VYQL-DOS-045, cpp/js,
#     zlib wire format), RecursionGuardIndexedByUnnormalizedKey
#     (VYQL-DOS-036, cpp, seven identifiers of one codebase),
#     RecursiveObjectParentResolveWithoutCycleGuard (VYQL-DOS-035, PHP),
#     GsonObjectTypeAdapterRecursiveRead (VYQL-DOS-016, Java, CWE-502),
#     NestedExtglobExpansionWithoutDepthLimit (VYQL-DOS-047, JS). The
#     generic CWE-400 progress rule VYQL-DOS-029 consumes an engine
#     numeric_parser.missing_progress_check analysis that a structural
#     token parser produces nowhere. code.UnboundedResourceOperation,
#     which the two hand-written Rust bindings emit, is config-shaped
#     (chunk-count/message-size sentinels and response caps) and would
#     only restate (1)-(3) with no judgment.
#
# This is the depth-budget family -- 1320 (C, self-recursion fact),
# 1612 (Python, budget bypassed by dispatch), 1634 (C++, explicit-stack
# push without a size bound) and pool ranks 1534/1554/1559/1572/1586 --
# in its Rust recursive-descent form. Extraction and resolution are NOT
# the blocker, measured on the real file: the USG carries the cycle
# (parse_fixes#ret FLOWS to its call sites and the recursive argument
# Arg#3687 FLOWS back into parse_fixes#param#input), so what is missing
# is a cross-procedural classification -- "is this call cycle bounded by
# a depth budget" -- which is new vocabulary over a new relation, not a
# localised construct the engine mishandles (1634's conclusion). A bare
# unbounded-recursion label is unshippable for the same reason 1320
# measured (165 function bodies in libzmq/src alone): recursion is
# Rust's ordinary tree-walk idiom. No definition change shipped.
#
# verify_current_expected: both forms reject -- nothing fires on either.
# When recursion-depth budget vocabulary lands, the unbounded form must
# flip to expect.

test "rank1697: the descent re-enters itself with no depth budget"
  lang rust
  file rulex-lib/src/parse/parsers.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  use nom::{
      branch::alt,
      combinator::{cut, map, opt},
      multi::{many0, many1},
      sequence::{pair, tuple},
      IResult,
  };

  pub(crate) struct Input<'i, 'b> {
      source: &'i str,
      tokens: &'b [(Token, Span)],
  }

  impl<'i, 'b> Input<'i, 'b> {
      pub(super) fn from(
          source: &'i str,
          tokens: &'b [(Token, Span)],
      ) -> Result<Self, ParseError> {
          Ok(Input { source, tokens })
      }
  }

  pub(crate) fn parse(source: &str) -> Result<Rule<'_>, ParseError> {
      let tokens = super::tokenize::tokenize(source);
      let input = Input::from(source, &tokens)?;

      let (rest, rules) = parse_modified(input)?;
      if rest.is_empty() {
          Ok(rules)
      } else {
          Err(ParseErrorKind::LeftoverTokens.at(rest.span()))
      }
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_modified<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      try_map2(
          pair(
              many0(alt((
                  map(
                      tuple((
                          "let",
                          cut(Token::Identifier),
                          cut(Token::Equals),
                          cut(parse_or),
                          cut(Token::Semicolon),
                      )),
                      |(stmt, span)| (stmt, span),
                  ),
              ))),
              parse_or,
          ),
          |(stmts, rule)| Ok(rule),
          nom::Err::Failure,
      )(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_or<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(separated_list0(Token::Pipe, parse_sequence), |mut rules| {
          if rules.len() == 1 {
              rules.pop().unwrap()
          } else {
              Alternation::new_rulex(rules)
          }
      })(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_sequence<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(many1(parse_fixes), |mut rules| rules.pop().unwrap())(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_fixes<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      alt((
          try_map(
              pair(Token::Not, opt(parse_fixes)),
              |(_, rule)| {
                  if let Some(mut rule) = rule {
                      rule.negate()?;
                      Ok(rule)
                  } else {
                      Err(ParseErrorKind::Expected("expression"))
                  }
              },
              nom::Err::Failure,
          ),
          map(pair(parse_lookaround, parse_modified), |((kind, span), rule)| {
              let span = span.join(rule.span());
              Rule::Lookaround(Box::new(Lookaround::new(rule, kind, span)))
          }),
          try_map2(
              pair(parse_atom, many0(parse_repetition)),
              |(rule, _)| Ok(rule),
              nom::Err::Failure,
          ),
      ))(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_group<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(
          pair(opt(parse_capture), tuple((Token::OpenParen, parse_modified, cut(Token::CloseParen)))),
          |(capture, (_, rule, _))| rule,
      )(input)
  }
  ```

test "rank1697: the fixed revision bounds every re-entry with a recursion budget"
  lang rust
  file rulex-lib/src/parse/parsers.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  use nom::{
      branch::alt,
      combinator::{cut, map, opt},
      multi::{many0, many1},
      sequence::{pair, tuple},
      IResult, Parser,
  };

  pub(crate) struct Input<'i, 'b> {
      source: &'i str,
      tokens: &'b [(Token, Span)],
      recursion: u16,
  }

  impl<'i, 'b> Input<'i, 'b> {
      pub(super) fn from(
          source: &'i str,
          tokens: &'b [(Token, Span)],
          recursion: u16,
      ) -> Result<Self, ParseError> {
          Ok(Input { source, tokens, recursion })
      }

      pub(super) fn recursion_start(&mut self) -> Result<(), ParseError> {
          self.recursion = self
              .recursion
              .checked_sub(1)
              .ok_or_else(|| ParseErrorKind::RecursionLimit.at(self.span()))?;
          Ok(())
      }

      pub(super) fn recursion_end(&mut self) {
          self.recursion += 1;
      }
  }

  pub(crate) fn parse(source: &str, recursion: u16) -> Result<Rule<'_>, ParseError> {
      let tokens = super::tokenize::tokenize(source);
      let input = Input::from(source, &tokens, recursion)?;

      let (rest, rules) = parse_modified(input)?;
      if rest.is_empty() {
          Ok(rules)
      } else {
          Err(ParseErrorKind::LeftoverTokens.at(rest.span()))
      }
  }

  fn recurse<'i, 'b, O>(
      mut parser: impl Parser<Input<'i, 'b>, O, ParseError>,
  ) -> impl FnMut(Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, O> {
      move |mut input| {
          input.recursion_start().map_err(nom::Err::Failure)?;

          match parser.parse(input) {
              Ok((mut input, output)) => {
                  input.recursion_end();
                  Ok((input, output))
              }
              Err(e) => Err(e),
          }
      }
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_modified<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      try_map2(
          pair(
              many0(alt((
                  map(
                      tuple((
                          "let",
                          cut(Token::Identifier),
                          cut(Token::Equals),
                          cut(recurse(parse_or)),
                          cut(Token::Semicolon),
                      )),
                      |(stmt, span)| (stmt, span),
                  ),
              ))),
              recurse(parse_or),
          ),
          |(stmts, rule)| Ok(rule),
          nom::Err::Failure,
      )(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_or<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(separated_list0(Token::Pipe, parse_sequence), |mut rules| {
          if rules.len() == 1 {
              rules.pop().unwrap()
          } else {
              Alternation::new_rulex(rules)
          }
      })(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_sequence<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(many1(parse_fixes), |mut rules| rules.pop().unwrap())(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_fixes<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      alt((
          try_map(
              pair(Token::Not, opt(recurse(parse_fixes))),
              |(_, rule)| {
                  if let Some(mut rule) = rule {
                      rule.negate()?;
                      Ok(rule)
                  } else {
                      Err(ParseErrorKind::Expected("expression"))
                  }
              },
              nom::Err::Failure,
          ),
          map(
              pair(parse_lookaround, recurse(parse_modified)),
              |((kind, span), rule)| {
                  let span = span.join(rule.span());
                  Rule::Lookaround(Box::new(Lookaround::new(rule, kind, span)))
              },
          ),
          try_map2(
              pair(parse_atom, many0(parse_repetition)),
              |(rule, _)| Ok(rule),
              nom::Err::Failure,
          ),
      ))(input)
  }

  pub(super) fn parse_group<'i, 'b>(input: Input<'i, 'b>) -> PResult<'i, 'b, Rule<'i>> {
      map(
          pair(
              opt(parse_capture),
              tuple((Token::OpenParen, recurse(parse_modified), cut(Token::CloseParen))),
          ),
          |(capture, (_, rule, _))| rule,
      )(input)
  }
  ```
